-off, not open to new ideas. So strengths: anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership. Concerns: show-off (maybe cooperation), not open to new ideas (adaptability). No info on stress resilience, reliability, communication. Mixed.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical), but weak memory for numbers (attention), makes nasty remarks about colleagues (crew cooperation, communication). So strengths: reliability, stress, technical. Concerns: memory, interpersonal.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality), keeps calm in crisis (stress), understands complicated technology (technical), difficulty communicating ideas (communication), regarded as egocentric (cooperation), not willing to further education (adaptability). So strengths: decision, stress, technical. Concerns: communication, egocentric, adaptability.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress/resilience), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical/decision), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but regarded as know-it-all (cooperation), has hot temper (crew cooperation, stress). So strengths: problem solving, concentration, responsibility. Concerns: temperament, know-it-all.\n\nWe need to pick a candidate with best overall fit. All have concerns. Which candidate has fewer serious concerns? B has nasty remarks - that's serious for crew cooperation. C has egocentric and communication difficulty - also serious. D has hot temper and know-it-all - also serious. A has show-off and not open to new ideas - also concerning but maybe less severe? Show-off could affect crew cooperation, not open to new ideas affects adaptability. No info on stress resilience, but maybe anticipation and leadership help. Might be okay.\n\nThus maybe Candidate A is best overall? But we have no evidence of reliability. B is conscientious (reliability) but interpersonal issues severe. D has responsibility but hot temper severe. So maybe A is best.\n\nWe can start by recommending Candidate A, citing strengths and acknowledging concerns, and propose to discuss others.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
